===Etymology===
From {{suf|en|blend|er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈblɛndɚ/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈblɛndə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-blender.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛndə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A machine [[outfitted]] with sharp [[blade]]s, for [[mash|mashing]], [[crush|crushing]]{{,}} or [[liquefy|liquefying]] food ingredients.
#: {{synonyms|en|liquidiser|liquidizer|vitamiser|q3=Australia|vitamizer|q4=Australia}}
#: {{hyponyms|en|immersion blender}}
#: {{cot|en|food processor|mixer}}
# {{lb|en|theatre}} A piece of [[fabric]] sewn into the front of a [[theatrical]] [[wig]] to make it blend in with the performer's natural hair.
#* '''2013''', Martha Ruskai, ‎Allison Lowery, ''Wig Making and Styling: A Complete Guide for Theatre & Film'' (page 80)
#*: A '''blender''' is added to a wig in the same way that a quick front is added. It can be added at the same time as the fronting lace is added or after the wig is completed.

